################ astral-sh/ty#4031
`closed=True` on TypedDicts accepted before 3.15 | CLOSED COMPLETED | created 2026-07-18 closed 2026-07-18T18:29:38Z | labels: bug,runtime semantics,typeddict | author A5rocks
--- body
### Summary

The following playground link uses `closed=True` despite being set to 3.14. It should not allow that:
```pycon
Python 3.14.2 (main, Dec  5 2025, 21:11:58) [Clang 21.1.4 ] on darwin
Type "help", "copyright", "credits" or "license" for more information.
>>> from typing import TypedDict
>>> class X(TypedDict, closed=True):
...     x: int
...
Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "<python-input-1>", line 1, in <module>
    class X(TypedDict, closed=True):
        x: int
TypeError: _TypedDictMeta.__new__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'closed'
```

Link: https://play.ty.dev/16ea6d67-7603-4a2e-a90c-b7f79e6ceb09

I think this should be allowed in typing-only files, but not at runtime. (it *is* a useful behavior and why limit it!)

### Version

5055442b5
